  <!-- Section: Official FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="section-py faq-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-tag">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Common Questions on Government Schemes</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Important guidelines regarding OTR registration, document renewal, income limits, and application cycles.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-accordion-grid">
        
        <details class="faq-item" open>
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>Is SchemeMatch free to use for students?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes, SchemeMatch is 100% free to use. There are no fees, subscriptions, or hidden charges. We do not collect banking credentials or application processing fees.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>What is OTR (One Time Registration) on the National Scholarship Portal (NSP)?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>OTR is a 14-digit unique number issued on scholarships.gov.in using Aadhaar face or OTP authentication. It simplifies applying for multiple central and state scholarships without re-entering personal data each year.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>Can I apply for more than one government scholarship at the same time?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>As per Ministry guidelines, a student can receive only ONE primary scholarship for maintenance/living allowance from the Central Government. However, you can often combine tuition fee reimbursements or state travel concessions with loan subsidies.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>Who is authorized to issue the Family Income Certificate?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The Income Certificate must be issued by a competent revenue authority—typically the Tehsildar, Sub-Divisional Magistrate (SDM), or District Collector. Affidavits on notary stamp paper are generally not accepted on official portals.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>Why does my bank account need to be linked to Aadhaar (NPCI Mapper)?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>All government scholarship disbursements are sent via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) through the Aadhaar Payment Bridge (APB). Your bank account must be actively seeded on the NPCI mapper, otherwise the funds transfer will fail.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

